{"step_index":2443,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:45:39Z","input_tokens":2995,"cache_read_tokens":163701,"output_tokens":1564,"thinking":"Phase 6 focuses on providing Python reference solutions for curated problems. Each solution necessitates review and testing against various cases before verification. Documentation including baseline and optimized approaches, complexity analysis (time and space), and algorithm explanations is required where appropriate.\n\n\nThe reference solution model will incorporate baseline and optimized approaches for each curated problem. For baseline solutions, details will encompass code, time and space complexity, a step-by-step explanation, identification of common pitfalls, and a proof of correctness. Optimized solutions will also include code and clear titles.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nFocus is on ensuring all solutions are thoroughly tested and verified through execution against a comprehensive suite of test cases. Consideration is being given to enriching the user interface by providing an educational guide alongside the code, including tabs or selectors for different solution approaches. The core goal is to generate verified, optimized Python solutions with detailed documentation.\n\n\nA structured approach is required for presenting curated solutions, encompassing baseline and optimized methods. Each solution will feature code examples, complexity analysis, and explanations, along with interactive elements for code execution and visualization. The system should generate this enriched content based on the problem input.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"import json; f=open('app_build/dsa_problems.js', encoding='utf-8').read(); idx=f.find('['); data=json.loads(f[idx:f.rfind(']')+1]);\nfor p in data[:10]:\n    print(f'#{p[\\\"id\\\"]} {p[\\\"title\\\"]} ({p[\\\"difficulty\\\"]}) - {p[\\\"pattern\\\"]}')\n\"","C