{"step_index":2453,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:18Z","input_tokens":2702,"cache_read_tokens":172271,"output_tokens":1937,"thinking":"Verified the successful execution of both baseline and optimized algorithms for maximum subarray and maximum profit problems. Step counts were validated against actual Python engine execution: demonstrating the expected algorithmic complexity differences ($O(n^2)$ vs. $O(n)$) between baseline and optimized solutions. This empirical data provides a clear illustration of performance gains from optimization.\n\n\nThe goal is to build a knowledge base of curated solutions, focusing on canonical problems. This will include both baseline and optimized approaches for core problems, detailing code, complexity analysis, and explanations. High-quality optimized solutions will be provided for other problems. The user interface will be updated to display these comprehensive solution cards upon request.\n\n\nDeveloped the UI components for displaying solution approaches, including tabs for baseline and optimized solutions, with dynamic switching based on problem ID. Added complexity analysis indicators and code interaction buttons (copy, visualize). Educational panels (algorithm explanation, correctness, pitfalls, and verification) are integrated within the solution display. Implemented event handlers to manage solution display and interaction events (switching approaches, copying code, visualizing, and hiding the solution).\n\n\nThe initial focus is on problems requiring dual solutions (baseline and optimized). Identified canonical problems suitable for demonstrating optimization strategies: \"Two Sum\", \"Contains Duplicate\", \"Valid Anagram\", \"Product of Array Except Self\", and \"Longest Consecutive Sequence\". These problems will serve as foundational examples. Now, I'll move on to building the solution data.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\app_build\\index.html","EndLine":180,"StartLine":150,"toolAction":"Viewing script tags in index.html","toolSummary":"Check script inclusion in index.html"}}]}
